      "text": "Bayer's \"universal\" typeface (1925) was geometric, lowercase-first, functionalist.\nThe Bauhaus questioned the necessity of capital letters as aesthetically arbitrary."
    },
    {
      "id": "01-BAUHAUS.md#027",
      "path": [
