        "module": "graphic-design",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[bauhaus]",
        "section": "graphic-design",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Bauhaus: Total Design and the School",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "DESSAU (1925-1932)\n  Tone: Rationalist, industrial, proto-corporate\n  New building designed by Gropius himself\n  Moholy-Nagy's machine aesthetic takes hold\n  Bayer's typography; steel furniture\n  Output: Industrial prototypes, mass-producible forms"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-BAUHAUS.md#035",
      "path": [
        "01-BAUHAUS.md"
