      "text": "```\n1933: Bauhaus closes\n      |\n      v\n+------------------------------------------+\n|  STAFF AND STUDENTS FLEE EUROPE          |\n|                                          |\n|  Moholy-Nagy -> Chicago (New Bauhaus,    |\n|                  1937 = Institute of     |\n|                  Design)                 |\n|                                          |\n|  Gropius -> Harvard Graduate School      |\n|             of Design (chair, 1937)      |\n|                                          |\n|  Mies van der Rohe -> IIT Chicago        |\n|             (Architecture dept, 1938)    |\n|                                          |\n|  Josef Albers -> Black Mountain College, |\n|             then Yale (1950)             |\n|                                          |\n|  Herbert Bayer -> NYC advertising /      |\n|             Aspen Institute              |\n+------------------------------------------+\n      |\n      v\nAmerican design education transforms:\n- Foundation courses become standard\n- Functional modernism becomes corporate house style\n- IBM, CBS, Container Corp hire Bauhaus-trained designers\n```"
    }
